# khaledzaky.com — Project Rules

## Project Overview
Personal website and blog for Khaled Zaky (Head of AI Governance & Evaluations Platform Engineering at RBC Borealis, within RBC's AI Group).
Built with Astro v7 + Tailwind CSS v4 (Node >=22.12). Deployed on AWS via CodeBuild → S3 → CloudFront.
Repo: https://github.com/kzaky/khaledzaky.com (branch: master)

---

## AI Blog Agent — Architecture Constants

### Lambda Functions (11 total)
Pipeline order: `research → draft → verify → evaluate → chart → notify → [HITL] → publish`
(Step Functions also has three Pass states that prune the payload: PruneBeforeEvaluate,
PruneBeforeCharts, PruneForRevise.)
Full list: `research`, `draft`, `verify`, `evaluate`, `chart`, `notify`, `approve`, `publish`, `ingest`, `upload`, `alarm-formatter`

### LLM Passes Per Lambda
**Research:** query generation (Haiku), Perplexity reshape (Haiku), editorial hooks and
thinking plan (Sonnet, parallel), synthesis (Opus, Sonnet fallback, 16000), cross-reference
fact-check (Sonnet), chart data extraction (Haiku).

**Draft (in order):** thinking plan (Sonnet) → full draft (Opus, Sonnet fallback, 16000) →
structure audit (Sonnet 16000) → chart + diagram placeholders (Sonnet) → citation review
(Sonnet 4000, read-only) → voice audit (Sonnet 16000) → `_lint_slop` (deterministic) →
insight + named-entity audits (Sonnet 16000 each, concurrent, skipped on revise).
Haiku only for category inference and a missing meta description.

**Verify:** one Haiku call per external link. Suggest-only by default (`VERIFY_AUTO_REPAIR=0`):
writes nothing into the post; findings go to the review email.

**Evaluate:** L0 gate, five rubric seats (taste seats on `JUDGE_MODEL_ID`, live value in
SSM `/blog-agent/models/judge`), at most one Sonnet repair.

**Notify:** five pre-HITL checks, Haiku intent check.

### Cost Estimate
Measured from Bedrock metrics (Oct 2026): ~$1.32 for a single-pass post, ~$2.26 for a
typical post with one revise. Perplexity adds ~$0.01/run; everything else is ~free tier.

### SSM Parameter Keys
- `/blog-agent/github-token` — GitHub PAT (SecureString)
- `/blog-agent/tavily-api-key` — Tavily search (SecureString)
- `/blog-agent/perplexity-api-key` — Perplexity sonar-pro (SecureString, optional — degrades gracefully)
- `/blog-agent/known-post-slugs` — String, kept current by Publish Lambda
- `/blog-agent/models/*` — model IDs (sonnet, opus, haiku, judge); source of truth for `deploy.sh`
- `cloudfront_distid` — CloudFront distribution ID (String, used by CodeBuild)

### Models
Defaults are in `agent/deploy.sh`; the live values are the `/blog-agent/models/*` SSM
parameters and each Lambda's environment. Opus for the two generation passes, Sonnet for
the audits, Haiku for mechanical passes, a non-Anthropic judge for the taste seats.

### Review findings
Draft lifts every review comment (INSIGHT, ENTITY CHECK, STRUCTURE, citation findings) out of
the post into the review email. Publish still strips any review annotation as a backstop.

### Key Files
- `agent/README.md` — full agent documentation
- `agent/template.yaml` — CloudFormation (all Lambda + Step Functions resources)
- `agent/deploy.sh` — one-command deployment
- `agent/voice-profile.sample.md` — format of the voice profile (the real profile is private, outside the repo)
- `agent/tests/test_handlers.py` — smoke tests; LAMBDA_DIRS must include all 11 Lambdas
- `agent/evals/` — hand-fix corpus and `run_gate.py`
- `RECOVERY.md` — disaster recovery runbook (**gitignored — kept privately**)
- `README.md` — root project documentation

### Infrastructure Notes
- CloudFormation stack: `blog-agent` (us-east-1)
- `DraftsBucketPolicy` managed outside CFN — do NOT add to template
- `ApproveApiRoute` is a single GET route — do NOT split into GET/POST
- CSP `connect-src` managed via CloudFront CLI (not CFN) — drift is intentional
- `infra/template.yaml` CSP is intentionally behind deployed state

---

## Documentation Invariants
When making ANY pipeline change, these must stay in sync:
1. Lambda count (11) referenced in `README.md`, `agent/README.md`, `template.yaml` comments
2. Pass order, token budgets and cost figures in both READMEs
3. Module docstrings in affected `index.py` files
4. `agent/tests/test_handlers.py` → `LAMBDA_DIRS` list
5. `RECOVERY.md` (kept privately, gitignored) → SSM secrets section + log retention loop
6. `agent/deploy.sh` → packaging loop, deploy loop, cleanup line, prerequisites

---

## Blog Post Tone
Khaled is a software and platform engineer learning the AI/ML space — NOT a deep academic expert.
Posts should sound like:
- Weekend research + curiosity, not authoritative treatises
- Personal reflection from 9-5 work experience
- "I've been thinking about..." not "It is well established that..."
- Explain jargon when used (e.g., MMLU needs a plain-English parenthetical)
- Avoid: BLEU, ROUGE, and other benchmarks the author doesn't claim to know deeply

---

## Public Repo Hygiene
This is a public portfolio repo. The following are **gitignored and kept privately**:
- `.windsurf/` — internal rules, workflows, architecture details
- `RECOVERY.md` — personal runbook with email address and operational details
- the voice profile — personal writing style guide (only `agent/voice-profile.sample.md` is public)

Safe to keep public (portfolio showcase):
- All `agent/*.py` Lambda source files
- `agent/template.yaml`, `agent/deploy.sh` — IaC and deployment automation
- `agent/README.md`, `README.md`, `infra/README.md` — use generic placeholder emails only
- `blog@khaledzaky.com` in blog posts — intentionally public, pipeline is protected by sender allowlist

Do NOT add personal emails, account IDs, API URLs or credentials for private tools, private
pages, the voice profile's location, or operational runbook details to tracked files.

---

## Commit Format
Use conventional commits:
- `feat:` new features
- `fix:` bug fixes
- `docs:` documentation only
- `refine:` editorial/tone changes to blog posts
- `infra:` infrastructure/CloudFormation changes
- `chore:` maintenance (deps, cleanup)

Always push to `master` after committing.
